      "value": "@{63ac197b13d3c4455e9b6768|full_name} what type of verification? that makes even less sense to me. That would mean we can't trust anymore who gave out the other badges? \n\nFor my understanding Badges should have been exactly for such markings. User and creator around VRChat can collect them, and have collected them for various creations so far. Like somebody in CE is no difference! Also other people have shown huge commitment, have contracts and so on.\n\nEmplyees are the most trust worhy. The most of them hiding on there profile that they are working for VRChat. And are allowed to. What about moderators of VRChat which are previledged with moderation permissions in instances?\n\nI have some cool badges on my profile, they should give me also extra \"trust\". Do i get such a checkmark too? I want to be verified too.\n\nWe all should be here on an even level and use Badges.\n\nAbout the original topic, forcing this on the Profile of VRChat's creator has a strong taste of \"user must see that they can pay money on this *personal* profile\".\n\nI could imagine that that the creator checkmark stays only as long as you are an active seller. While it would support my previous point. I think that would also be wrong to do, As a creator who sold on the Marketplace, you should keep the badge.\n\nYou made a big change on the platform. Badges can look different by type/level/flair/contribution-year/..., creator should have this customizability too, to show what they have reached in versatility and creativity.\n\nTLDR; this should atleast get a toggle, or better replaced with a badge.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
