      "value": "@{63ac197b13d3c4455e9b6768|full_name} I strongly believe Players have the same freedom as a developer, Creators do sell content, Some creators promote it, Some just list it and don't talk about it.\n\nEvery creator has a different methored of how they operate, Just like every other user wanting to hide their VRC+ gifting badges to prevent someone badgering them asking for a vrc+ gift.\n\nBefore this update Nobody would have known that 1 person is a seller unless they have phyiscally seen their content, Hard-forcing the display of users being a creator to VRChat goes against the fundamentals of the badge system, Badges are Your public display pin, You get 3 main ones to show everyone no matter what they are. (Freedom of choice)\n\nNow Changing that system by creating Tags, when there’s a perfectly good system where the User always has the option to hide or show their badges letting the user always decide their comfort level.\n\nI Seriously disagree that a VRChat developer hiding their badge is different to a normal user hiding their creator status, They are both a form of employment/proactive engagement with the platform and Stripping users of that permission ruins the freedom of choice badges has always given us.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
